4. **User Feedback**: Provide meaningful feedback to users if there are errors during user-related operations (e.g., login, registration). Validating input thoroughly before attempting to interact with data can prevent many common errors related to user input.

5. **Initialization Logic**: Structure application initialization logic in a clear and reliable way to ensure that all necessary components and configurations are set up before starting the app. This reduces the chances of running into `connection refused` errors due to misconfigurations or missing initializations.

6. **Testing Deployments**: Regularly deploy testing builds and verify that all components are functional within a staging environment. Ensuring that the Flask application can be started and verified separately from tests helps isolate issues that may arise only during automated testing.

By focusing on these areas during development, the likelihood of encountering similar startup issues and managing user interactions effectively can be reduced in future iterations of the project.|
